    <tags>shader-cache gpu nvidia amd intel gaming cleanup discord steam epic portable</tags>
    <summary>Clear GPU, Windows and game launcher caches in one click.</summary>
    <description>
ShaderSweep clears the shader caches your graphics driver and Windows build up, plus the caches of game launchers such as Discord, Steam, Epic Games Launcher and Battle.net, and a few Windows housekeeping items.

It scans first and shows every cache with its size before anything is deleted, notices when a new GPU driver arrives, names the program holding any file it cannot remove, and checks after a restart that Windows really removed the files it queued.

Only folders on a fixed list of regenerable caches are ever touched. Logins, settings and installed games are not.

The app asks for administrator rights when it starts, because some caches belong to system accounts. It also has a headless mode: ShaderSweep --clean --preview
    </description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/Kkthnx/ShaderSweep/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md</releaseNotes>
